# Compact mobile layout

Screens are used on a phone. Extra headings make people scroll. One header is enough.

Superadmin on a desktop (`md` and up) may use a sidebar and extra columns. Compact rules still apply on phones and for every other role. Do not add `FormSection` titles or a subtitle line under the page title.

## Page header

- Use a single header line (`PageHeader` title only).
- Do not add a subtitle on its own line under the title.
- If something matters (group name, status), put it on that same line in smaller type.

```tsx
// Bad — title, then a second line
<PageHeader title="Fellowship Report" subtitle={group.name} />

// Good — one line; extra context is smaller, on the same line
<header>
  <h1>
    Fellowship Report <span className="text-sm font-normal text-slate-500">{group.name}</span>
  </h1>
</header>
```

## Sections

- Do not add titled subsections (`FormSection` headings) above fields that already have labels. "Attendance" over "Attendees" is a header and a subheader.
- Do not repeat the idea: page title, then section title, then field label.
- Put a short note on the same label row in smaller type (`Field` `aside`). Do not add a hint line under the control for that note.
- Keep short related inputs on one row. A new block is only for content that needs the height (a textarea, photos).
- Country and number share one “Mobile number” row. Date and time share one “Date & Time” row.

```tsx
// Bad — section heading plus field labels, each adding height
<FormSection title="Attendance">
  <Field label="Attendees">...</Field>
  <Field label="First-time">...</Field>
</FormSection>

// Good — the field label is the only heading; a note stays on that line
<div className="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
  <Field label="Attendees" aside="Planned: 12">...</Field>
  <Field label="First-time">...</Field>
</div>
```
